Eq. 3.3 Minimum Resolution Threshold (Foundational): Below-threshold invocations fail quietly rather than backlashing
if Fid < Fid_min:  X_eff ~ 0   (fails quietly — not a backlash)
where Fid: Fidelity coefficient — overlap between ideal and actual invocation; Fid_min: Minimum fidelity below which an invocation fails to manifest; X_eff: Theoretical output of a fully solved term, and the effective output actually produced — X_ideal scaled by Fid; a(t): Amplitudes: "still at A" / "arrived at B"
